::SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.06
Question:
Word origins and derivations item 1: Which choice best uses word-family knowledge for speech vocabulary?
{
~A. Guess the meaning from sound alone#This choice is too vague or informal for the speech purpose. Choose language that supports audience understanding.
~B. Use the same word form in every sentence#This choice may sound related, but it does not show precise vocabulary control for communication.
=C. Use related word forms correctly in a speech sentence#Correct. This choice uses vocabulary knowledge to make the speech clearer, more precise, and appropriate for the audience.
~D. Choose a made-up word form#This choice weakens the speech because it does not make the speaker language clearer or more precise.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.05
Question:
Word origins and derivations item 2: Which choice best uses word-family knowledge for speech vocabulary?
{
=A. Explain a speech term by connecting root meaning and context#Correct. This choice uses vocabulary knowledge to make the speech clearer, more precise, and appropriate for the audience.
~B. Use the same word form in every sentence#This choice may sound related, but it does not show precise vocabulary control for communication.
~C. Ignore context when explaining the word#This choice reflects a misconception about word meaning or word origin. Use context and meaning to revise.
~D. Choose a made-up word form#This choice weakens the speech because it does not make the speaker language clearer or more precise.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q03::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L04_Quiz_Q03
